# Video Auto Tool (VAT) - project rules

## What this is
Windows desktop app (C# / .NET 8 / WPF) that batch-produces videos with ffmpeg from a designed template:
audio from source videos + looping backgrounds + avatar + soundwave + burned-in subtitles.
Full spec: `docs/SPEC.md` (read ONLY the sections relevant to the current task, do not load the whole file).
Handoff/progress log: `docs/PROGRESS.md` (READ IT FIRST in every new chat; UPDATE IT at the end of every task).

## Language
- Reply to the user in Vietnamese. Keep answers short and concrete.
- Code, identifiers, code comments, commit messages, log messages: English.
- User-facing UI strings: Vietnamese, kept in `Resources/Strings.vi.resx` (never hard-coded in XAML/code-behind).

## Stack (do not add packages without asking)
- .NET 8, C# 12, `<Nullable>enable</Nullable>`, `<TreatWarningsAsErrors>true</TreatWarningsAsErrors>` for Core.
- WPF + CommunityToolkit.Mvvm (MVVM). System.Text.Json. xUnit for tests. SkiaSharp (tests and text measuring).
- FFmpeg is an EXTERNAL executable (ffmpeg.exe / ffprobe.exe). Never link ffmpeg libraries.

## Solution layout
- `src/VideoAutoTool.Core`  - all logic, ZERO UI references.
- `src/VideoAutoTool.Cli`   - console front-end (`vat`) used to test Core headless.
- `src/VideoAutoTool.App`   - WPF UI only. No business logic in code-behind.
- `tests/VideoAutoTool.Core.Tests` - xUnit tests. `scripts/` - PowerShell helpers. `testdata/` - generated, git-ignored.

## Commands
- Build: `dotnet build`  |  Test: `dotnet test`
- CLI: `dotnet run --project src/VideoAutoTool.Cli -- <command>`
- Test data: `pwsh scripts/make-testdata.ps1`

## Coding rules
- Every long operation is `async` with `CancellationToken` and `IProgress<T>`. Never block the UI thread.
- Call external processes ONLY through `FfmpegRunner` using `ProcessStartInfo.ArgumentList` (never a joined command string).
- Must work with paths containing spaces, emoji and Vietnamese characters. Use `Path.Combine`; no hard-coded absolute paths.
- Deterministic planning: same inputs => same plan (no `DateTime.Now`/unseeded random in planning).
- Errors: return typed results / throw specific exceptions; never swallow exceptions silently. Log through `ILog`.
- Keep diffs small and focused. Do NOT refactor unrelated code. Ask before changing architecture or adding a package.
- Prefer pointing to canonical examples in the repo over inventing new patterns.

## Definition of done (for every task)
1. `dotnet build` has 0 warnings/errors and `dotnet test` passes - actually RUN them, never claim success without running.
2. New public Core behavior has unit tests (see acceptance criteria in the task).
3. `docs/PROGRESS.md` updated (what was done, decisions, open issues, next step).
4. Final message to the user: what changed, how to try it (exact command), what is NOT done or unverified.

